SLUG: terms.html
TITLE: Terms of Service | Akash Movers, Kanpur
DESC: The terms covering quotes, bookings, your responsibilities, items we cannot carry, liability and claims, storage and payment for moving services.
HEADING: Terms of service
LEAD: The terms that apply to quotes and bookings. Several sections need the business's own figures before this page is published — they are marked.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Terms|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow flow">

        <div class="demo-banner">
          <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-alert"/></svg>
          <div>
            <strong>Template — not ready to publish.</strong>
            Every section marked <em>[TO BE SUPPLIED]</em> needs the business's
            real policy, and the whole page needs a legal review before it goes
            live. Numbers have deliberately been left blank rather than filled
            with plausible-looking defaults: a cancellation fee or a liability
            cap invented by a website is unenforceable at best and misleading
            at worst. Remove this notice once the page is complete and checked.
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2>1. Who these terms are between</h2>
        <p>
          These terms apply between
          <strong data-config="business.name">the company</strong> and the
          customer requesting or booking moving services. Submitting an
          enquiry does not create a booking; a booking exists once we have
          confirmed it in writing.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Quotes and estimates</h2>
        <p>
          A quote is based on the inventory and access described during the
          survey. It is valid for the period stated on the quote itself.
        </p>
        <p>
          If, on the day, the goods or the access differ materially from what
          was described — significantly more items, a floor or lift situation
          not disclosed, or a carry distance substantially longer than agreed
          — we will set out the revised cost and obtain your approval before
          continuing. We will not complete the work and present a different
          figure afterwards.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Booking, rescheduling and cancellation</h2>
        <p><em>[TO BE SUPPLIED]</em> — the business must state:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>What, if anything, is payable to confirm a booking</li>
          <li>How much notice is needed to reschedule without a charge</li>
          <li>The cancellation terms, and at what point a charge applies</li>
          <li>What happens if we have to reschedule, and what you are entitled to</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. What we need from you</h2>
        <p>To do the job properly we need you to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Describe the inventory and the access accurately at survey</li>
          <li>Obtain any building or society permission needed for the move</li>
          <li>Be present, or have an authorised adult present, at both addresses</li>
          <li>Carry jewellery, cash, documents and other high-value small items yourself</li>
          <li>Empty and disconnect gas cylinders, and defrost and drain appliances, before the day</li>
          <li>Check the inventory against the goods at delivery and note anything wrong on the sheet before the crew leaves</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Items we cannot carry</h2>
        <p>
          We do not transport cash, jewellery, government documents,
          firearms, hazardous or flammable goods, loaded gas cylinders,
          perishable food, illegal items, or live animals. Pets should travel
          with you. Plants can be carried on local moves but travel poorly
          over long distances, and we will tell you so rather than take the
          booking.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Liability and claims</h2>
        <p><em>[TO BE SUPPLIED]</em> — the business must state:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The transit cover options actually offered, and what each covers</li>
          <li>Any limit of liability, and how it is calculated</li>
          <li>The window for reporting damage or loss after delivery</li>
          <li>The documents required to make a claim, and the timeline for a decision</li>
          <li>What is excluded — for example goods packed by the customer, or pre-existing damage</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Until those are supplied, nothing on this website should be read as
          a promise of insurance or compensation. Ask for the cover terms in
          writing with your quote.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Storage</h2>
        <p>
          Where goods are held in storage, they are inventoried in and out and
          charged by duration, separately from the move. The applicable rate
          and billing period are confirmed in writing before anything enters
          the facility. <em>[TO BE SUPPLIED]</em> — notice required to release
          goods, and what happens if storage charges fall into arrears.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Payment</h2>
        <p><em>[TO BE SUPPLIED]</em> — accepted payment methods, when payment is
        due relative to loading and delivery, whether any part is payable in
        advance, and what applies to late payment.</p>

        <h2>9. Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          Raise any problem with your coordinator first — most things are
          fixed fastest while the crew is still on site. If it is not
          resolved, contact us through the
          <a href="/contact.html">contact page</a>.
          <em>[TO BE SUPPLIED]</em> — escalation contact and the time within
          which complaints are acknowledged.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts at
          <em>[TO BE SUPPLIED — city]</em> have jurisdiction.
        </p>

        <p class="form-note mt-7">
          Last updated <time data-updated-date>11 October 2026</time>.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
